# Document memory limits

Every `MemoryMax`, `MemoryHigh`, and `GOMEMLIMIT` must be listed in
[docs/memory.md](docs/memory.md) so host RAM is a sum, not a guess.

- Add or update the row when you introduce or change a limit. Include the
  unit, the host(s), and why the cap exists (OOM blast radius, 1 GiB hub,
  compaction headroom).
- Also mention the limit on the service doc. Host-only overrides belong
  on the host doc and in the inventory.
- Before raising a cap, check live RSS against `MemoryMax` and the host's
  remaining RAM. Do not raise Mimir/Loki/Vector without that
  (`docs/services/mimir.md`, `docs/adr/2026-09-04-xcloud-postgres-1g.md`).
- A service without a limit is still a RAM consumer: note large heaps
  (`shared_buffers`, JVM, Grafana) on the same inventory.
